; The fractional `.fff` tail is all-or-nothing — exactly 3 digits.
; `.1` is not 3 digits, so the lexer emits a `time` token for the
; 8-char prefix and leaves `.1` for the next pass (which produces
; a `.1` number token). The parser walks both tokens cleanly with
; no diagnostics; downstream consumers see two roots — one time,
; one number.
12:34:56.1
